      "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $1\\,050$ and $245.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}1050 & = & 245(4) & + & 70 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 245 & = & 70(3) & + & 35 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 70 & = & 35(2) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $35.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $1\\,050$ and $245$ is $35.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(1\\,050,245)=35.\n$$",
